      "excerpt": " log P ( x ) . (3.48) In this b o ok, we alwa ys use log to mean the natural logarithm, with base e . Our deﬁnition of I ( x ) is therefore written in units of nats . One nat is the amount of information gained by observing an even t of probability 1 e . Other texts use base-2 71 CHA",
